  "id": "mental-practice",
  "term": "mental practice",
  "definition": "Mental practice is a training method that uses repeated motor imagery, meaning mentally simulating a movement, to improve actual motor performance. In rehabilitation and motor learning contexts, it is used as a simple, low-cost way to rehearse actions without physically performing them.",
